{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This is the statute of the Torah.</b> A statute of the laws of impurity. And it was stated on the first of Nisan, the day the Tabernacle was erected, because on the next day the cow was burned, so that they would be purified for their Paschal offerings. And beforehand they could not perform it, for we require ״and he shall sprinkle toward the front of the Tent of Meeting״ (v. 4), and there was none. Even so, it was written here because there were among them those impure through corpse-contact, from the dispute of Korah." "<b>Which YHWH commanded.</b> We do not find where this commandment was explicitly stated in another place, as he explained above in the perasha of בא." "<b>And they shall take to you.</b> Since it is stated ״you and your sons with you shall bear the iniquity of your priesthood״ (Num. 18:1), Scripture tells that on their account it comes from their own property. And so it is written ״and you shall give it to Elazar the priest״ (v. 4) — it is a gift to him from public property."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:35.370350444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}